N.D. Ind. L.P.R. 2-1 Scheduling, Discovery, and Orders
(a) Scheduling Conference. The court will hold a scheduling conference within 30 days 
after the last answer is filed.
(b) Discovery Plan. The parties must comply with Fed. R. Civ. P. 26(f) before the 
conference. Their discovery plan must address these topics:
• Date/place of conference;
• Counsel present/parties represented;
• Case summary;
• Jurisdictional questions;
• Type of trial;
• Discovery needed;
• Electronic-information disclosures;
• Stipulation regarding privilege claims/protecting trial-preparation materials;
• Interrogatories;
• Requests for admission;
• Depositions;
• Joinder of additional parties;
• Amending pleadings; and
• Settlement possibilities/mediation.
